the green ribbons of this long  campaign for justice may be fading  but this mother is clear about where she  wants to go  next she's bringing a civil claim for  damages against the american woman  accused of causing her son's death  it may well be the only justice we get  but it's  it's not the only justice that we want  we obviously want her to face the  criminal justice system as well and that  is still  our number one without a doubt is still  our number one  teenager harry dunn was killed in a  collision with  former cia agent anserkulas in august  2019.  it happened outside the american  intelligence base  raf croton in northamptonshire  she left the uk claiming diplomatic  immunity  but was later charged with causing death  by dangerous driving  the trump administration has refused to  extradite her  now the foreign secretary dominic raab  has written to harry's parents  he said i strongly support your right to  bring  this case as you know we have offered  support to allow you to attend the  hearings in virginia  and i understand other witnesses are  also ready to go to the u s  we've had mr rob and  his aides tell us for a year or so now  that  they are on our side that they're  supporting us that they're  they're doing everything that they can  but this  letter is the first piece of written  evidence that we've seen  that actually backs up that claim  not only is mrs sakulas refusing to  return to the uk to face  trial her legal team is disputing that  harry's family can take action in  virginia  mrs sakulasa's home state  without an extradition the family only  have a limited number of legal options  it's obviously very unusual for the  foreign secretary to  back an individual bringing a claim  in a foreign country but dominic raab  clearly thinks the united states  should have waived and secured his  immunity given that they didn't  the family have no choice as far as they  can see it  but to take a civil claim in the united  states against her  harry's family will find out in january  if the case can go ahead  in america lisa dowd sky news  northamptonshire
 

